    "summary": "High-energy set with scorching Throwing Stones and epic Other One",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering first set and a second‑set marathon featuring a fiery Throwing Stones, an unmissable The Other One, and a special Santa Fe verse in Never Trust A Woman. Jerry’s vocals and guitar are on fire, Phil drives the band with powerful bass, and Brent adds tasteful slide work.",
    "review": "On October 17, 1982, the Dead turned Santa Fe Downs into a high‑octane playground. The first set surged from Mississippi Half‑Step straight into Let It Grow, laying down a tight groove that kept the crowd locked in. The second set lifted off after the classic drums‑and‑space stretch, launching into an unstoppable Throwing Stones that roared through the night and a marathon The Other One that felt like two shows in one. Highlights included a Santa Fe‑only verse of Never Trust A Woman, a soaring Good Lovin', and a heartfelt ballad moment from Jerry later in the set. Across all three audience recordings, reviewers rave about the band's locked‑in energy, Jerry’s scorching guitar tone, Phil’s roaring bass on The Other One, and Brent’s tasteful slide touches – making this night a standout entry in the early‑’80s catalog.\n\nWhile the tapes are audience sources with occasional glitches (a brief cut in Althea and some drop‑outs), the upgraded recording captures enough clarity to let listeners feel the fire. For Deadheads seeking the definitive version of this high‑energy performance, the Miller audience tape “gd82-10-17.fob-aud.miller.18108.sbeok.shnf” offers the most complete and vivid listening experience.",
